  "question": {
    "text": "Let the determinant of a square matrix <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;of order <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi></math>, where m and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> satisfy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>22</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>17</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>93</mn></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi></msup><msup><mn>5</mn><mi>b</mi></msup><msup><mn>6</mn><mi>c</mi></msup></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
